+// SetEarlyStop turns the engine's stability cut-off on or off. FORK addition.
+//
+// Upstream ends a phase as soon as the rate has been stable for a third of a
+// 5 s window, with a floor of minSteps = 2 x windowSize. In practice that means
+// EVERY phase ends at ~10 s no matter what capture time was asked for — measured
+// on 2026-08-19/20, where a requested 15 s produced an actual 10.1 s in seven
+// runs out of seven.
+//
+// That is fine for "how fast is my line right now" and fatal for a comparison:
+// a fixed measurement window is exactly what makes runs at different thread
+// counts comparable, and it cannot be had while the engine decides for itself
+// when it has seen enough. Research mode turns the cut-off off; ordinary runs
+// leave it on, because for them stopping early is a feature.
+func (dm *DataManager) SetEarlyStop(enabled bool) Manager {
+	dm.noEarlyStop = !enabled
+	return dm
+}
